 "deepDive": {
  "domain": "Law, courts & regulation",
  "title": "What happens next in the Kraków case, legally",
  "body": "Prosecutors have opened the investigation as a **terrorist act**. That label has legal effects. The Criminal Code (art. 115 §20) defines a terrorist offence as a crime punishable by at least five years that is committed to seriously intimidate many people, to force public authorities to act or refrain, or to seriously disrupt the state or economy. The classification affects who leads the case and which aggravating rules apply. It also shapes how the state talks about the attack, which is why the interior minister's early remarks about the suspect's views have become [politically contested](https://tvrepublika.pl/Polityka/Insynuacje-szefa-MSWiA-Kierwinski-zaczyna-ideologiczna-gre-wokol-tragedii/225426).\n\n**Sequence.** Formal charges (*postawienie zarzutów*) need the suspect to be questioned, and he is in critical condition. Prosecutors say they will wait for doctors, then charge him, question him and ask a court for a preventive measure, almost certainly pre-trial detention ([Polsat News](https://www.polsatnews.pl/wiadomosc/2026-11-08/czyn-o-charakterze-terrorystycznym-ruch-prokuratury-po-tragedii-w-krakowie/)). Killing several people in one act is among the offences carrying Poland's heaviest penalty, **life imprisonment**. The three deaths at his family home in Ostrowiec are handled within the same investigation.\n\n**The gun question.** Reports say the suspect held his weapons legally under a sport-shooting permit ([Interia](https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/malopolskie/news-co-wiemy-o-ataku-na-rynku-glownym-w-krakowie-najwazniejsze-i,nId,23570696)). A 2025 audit by the Supreme Audit Office (NIK) found the number of legally held firearms rising fast and police supervision of permit holders weak ([NIK](https://www.nik.gov.pl/en/news/more-and-more-firearms-in-use-and-poor-supervision.html)). Expect proposals on medical and psychological checks and on sport permits; no draft has been tabled yet.\n\n**What to watch:** the date of charges, any change to the legal classification, and whether the government or Sejm introduces firearms changes once mourning ends.",
  "links": [
   {
    "label": "Polsat News",
    "url": "https://www.polsatnews.pl/wiadomosc/2026-11-08/czyn-o-charakterze-terrorystycznym-ruch-prokuratury-po-tragedii-w-krakowie/"
   },
   {
    "label": "NIK audit",
    "url": "https://www.nik.gov.pl/en/news/more-and-more-firearms-in-use-and-poor-supervision.html"
   }
  ]
 },
